ker to go on a rampage after being  denied a final clash with his  arch-nemesis long before that however  Bruce and selina had a child together  her name was Hellena Wayne and as you  might expect it wasn't long before she  joined the family business as a crime  fighter she took the name Huntress and  wore costume that combined Batman's  pointy-eared look with cat woman's  traditional purple what might be  surprising though is that she wasn't the  kind of prominent character you'd expect  Batman and Catwoman daughter to become  while she started a few stories and  fought crime alongside the grown up  Robin as the new  dynamic duo Elena Wayans most prominent  appearances came when she took an  interdimensional vacation to earth one  to spend some time with that world's  version of her dad of course meeting up  with the alternate reality daughter you  fathered with the supervillain is always  going to be a little weird but you know  it's the DC Universe you get used to  stuff like that by the mid-80s DC's  multiverse had expanded well beyond  Earth to into a whole roster of  alternate worlds built around different  ideas one where the Nazis won World War  two when where Kennedy was never  assassinated a what one where all of us  are evil been there it sucks in 1985  they tried to clean it all up with a 12  issue events called crisis on Infinite  Earths the ads for the series claim that  worlds will live worlds will die and the  DC Universe will never be the same  and while comic books have often  featured some tag lines that went way  over the top this one actually lived up  to it the main effect of the story was  that the multiverse of parallel worlds  was obliterated and streamlined into a  single unified timeline as a result  there was no more earth to Batman  because there was no more earth to to be  the Batman up if earth - didn't exist  then neither did Helene at Wayne it's  worth noting that Huntress was one of  the few characters to survive the  initial destruction of her home to  mention finding herself stranded  alongside her Earth's Robin on a strange  world with no record of her existence  with nothing left for her in the  universe she joined Robin on a final  fatal mission the final indignity the  story specifically states that her body  and Robins were never recovered after  their deaths here's the thing about  superhero comics nothing ever really  goes away  especially when it's tied to a character  as prominent as Batman with that in mind  it's no surprise that DC brought back  the Huntress only a few years after  crisis what is surprising is that they  completely reinvented the character in  almost every aspect aside from her  costume and her first name and even the  costume underwent some radical changes  before too long  instead of being Batman's daughter the  post-crisis Huntress was something a  little closer to being DC's take on the  Punisher Helena Bertinelli was the  youngest member of one of Gotham C's  most prominent mobster families in the  years before Batman arrived and  organized crime was mostly replaced by  evil clowns and mad scientist's with ice  guns when she was only eight years old  Alana's entire family was murdered in  front of her by a hitman who left  live is the only survivor milena was  taken in by her family and Sicily who  offered the trainer so that she could  get a revenge something that she took to  very well when she returned to Gotham  however she saw Batman in action and  realized that if she really wanted to  strike terror in the hearts of the  mobsters who had targeted her family she  should follow in his footsteps as a  vigilante with that she took the  identity of the Huntress although that  wasn't her only calling while she was  wealthy enough to live off her family's  ill-gotten gains she actually kept a day  job as a schoolteacher something that  would have more prominence and other  versions of the character you don't  really get to be a vigilante in Gotham  City without attracting some attention  from be vigilante in Gotham City  sure enough the new Huntress soon  encountered Batman the big sticking  point between the two characters comes  from the way they deal with their  enemies most versions of Batman famously  have a code against killing the Huntress  on the other hand has no problem at all  sending her opponents off to their final  reward still Batman didn't set out to  take the Huntress down after all if  there's one person who understands the  intense trauma of watching your family  get gunned down in front of you and the  anger that can lead you to put on a  costume and wage work and stalked  criminals by night it's that guy still  he didn't approve of her methods but the  solution he came up with for this  particular problem wasn't the one that  anyone expected he let her join the  Justice League  Batman's hope was that membership in the  JLA surrounded by Paragons of virtue  like Superman and Wonder Woman would be  a good influence on the Huntress and  show her a different way of fighting  crime it did not work when Batman found  her getting ready to execute a helpless  super villain at the climax of one of  the league's biggest crises he booted  her out of the league in disappointment  Hellena Bertinelli's relationship with  the rest of the Batman family is a  little complicated we've already been  through her rocky interactions with the  Dark Knight himself but his sidekicks  tend to have a very different  perspective on Huntress Tim Drake for  instance had the sort of relationship  you'd expect from a super smart teenage  overachiever and a world-weary teacher  her relationship with Dick Grayson  better known as Nightwing is a little  more mature when he first encountered  the Huntress they had immediate  chemistry and they quickly found  themselves in a team-up with benefits an  actual relationship didn't blossom out  of that encounter though partly because  of the time that Huntress  accidentally shot Batman with 